1. Behind The Wings: The Case of Reverse Engineering and Drone Hijacking in DJI Enhanced Wi-Fi Protocol — D. Pratma, at al. - August 2024
		a. Summary: The paper investigates security weaknesses in the Enhanced Wi-Fi protocol used for drone control. Researchers reverse-engineered the protocol’s control commands and found vulnerabilities that could allow an attacker to hijack a drone’s communications and alter its flight path. They demonstrated the attack on a DJI Mini SE, showing that even inexpensive, commercially available Wi-Fi routers could be used to intercept and manipulate control commands. The research highlights the need for stronger UAV communication security, particularly as civilian drones are increasingly used in both civilian and military contexts.
		b. DOI Link: https://doi.org/10.1109/PlatCon63925.2024.10830741
	
